          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಅಳುಕು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಳುಕು — aḷuku — \"to waver; to flinch\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕತ್ತಲೆಯ ದಾರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಹೋಗಲು ನಾನು ಅಳುಕಿದೆ. kattaleya dāriyalli hōgalu nānu aḷukide. I flinched at going down the dark road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಅಳುಕಿದೆ, aḷukide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often negative: ಅಳುಕದೆ, without flinching."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಳುಕು (aḷuku) is native Dravidian: DEDR 306 lists Kannada aḷuku, \"to fear\", beside Tamil aḷukku, \"to be frightened\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
